    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259-a5">

                <pb facs="0320" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg252"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Moustier to Mr. Dix</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 15, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">General:</hi> I received the letter which you did me
                    the honor to write on the 8th of this month, transmitting a copy of an address
                    signed by a large number of citizens of the United States on the occasion of the
                    criminal attempt of the 6th of June. I hastened to place this communication
                    before the Emperor, who was greatly affected by it, and I conform to his orders
                    in conveying to you the expression of his Majesty’s sincere thanks.</p>
                <p>Accept assurances of the high consideration with which I have the honor to be,
                    general, your very humble and very obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MOUSTIER.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dix</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Minister of the United States, Paris.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
